   347	> **THEOREM AT THE STATED SCOPE:** family-wide D25 EMPTY proves that every D23 survivor was a finite-depth mirage and that no mod $p$ formal germ exists on the residue-A, B-frozen, no-log, `PIN42`, $W_1W_2\ne0$ chart at that prime and the atlas's fixed $r_3$ embedding.
   348	
   349	This kill direction uses neither valuation $e$, CYCLIC-30, nor E-HENSEL. One empty component kills only that component. A union-level NONEMPTY result does not show that all components survive, which is why the 36-bit mask is mandatory.
   350	
   351	D25 EMPTY is the point at which the residue-A kill campaign **resumes**, not the point at which a characteristic-zero theorem may already be announced. Repeat the exhaustive family calculation at a second good prime, then seek an exact $\mathbf Q(\sqrt3)$ identity with source-row provenance and discharge the conjugate $r_3$ embedding, other charts, no-log/`PIN42` coverage, and B-unfreezing. Modular emptiness alone is a screening-tier result.
   352	
   353	### 3.2 D25 NONEMPTY
   354	
   355	D25 NONEMPTY proves only that at least one point of $V_{25}$ projects to the D23 survivor locus. It deepens finite-window survival; it does not produce an inverse-limit point, a formal germ, a characteristic-zero germ, an algebraic branch, or a polynomial Keller pair.
   356	
   357	For every surviving component, record the image and fiber dimensions of
   358	
   359	\[
   360	 \pi_{25,23}:V_{25,\lambda}\longrightarrow V_{23,\lambda}.
   361	\]
   362	
   363	A severe image contraction is useful mirage evidence, while a positive-dimensional image shared across the coefficient classes is germ-track evidence. Neither is a theorem about infinite depth.
   364	
   365	### 3.3 The corrected $e$-test at D25
   366	
   367	The D25 threshold is
   368	
   369	\[
   370	 \left\lfloor\frac{25-1}{2}\right\rfloor=12.
   371	\]
   372	
   373	Recompute the exact low-band part of $L_s^+$ at genuine reconstructed D25 points using the true deep labels. A finite D25 point does **not** determine its $t^{42+}$ x-side completion. Before following $H_{29}$ beyond its first coefficient, do one of three things: use a sufficiently long explicitly compatible lift that supplies every coefficient consumed; prove a finite-range invariance lemma; or retain and quantify over the unspecified completion variables. Never silently zero-fill them.
   374	
   375	Track compatible points
   376	
   377	\[
   378	 s_{25}\leftarrow s_{27}\leftarrow s_{29}\leftarrow\cdots,
   379	\]
   380	
   381	not unrelated random witnesses or unrelated zero completions. Only an all-depth compatible chain, or a proved finite-determinacy result, supplies an all-depth operator.
   382	
   383	| corrected D25 behavior | exact conclusion |
   384	|---|---|
   385	| A **promoted** $e^+(s)\le12$, with CYCLIC-30, an exact delayed parametrix, the completed-ideal bridge, and E-HENSEL banked | A mod $p$ formal germ exists: decisive germ-track. |
   386	| A stable, internally consistent `E_CANDIDATE^+ <= 12` with measured \(\ell^+\le12\) | Strong germ-track evidence; no theorem. |
   387	| Finite promoted $e^+(s)>12$ | D25 is too shallow; target $D=2e^+(s)+1$. |
   388	| Certified \(\ell^+(s)>12\) | This point cannot supply a D25 Hensel certificate; it may still extend singularly. |
   389	| Drifting/unbounded \(\delta^+(N)\), resonance, or $e^+=\infty$ | Mirage-like or singular-track behavior; not a kill. |
   390	| Some later exact window is EMPTY | Definitive finite-depth mirage. |
   391	
   392	Thus a small promoted $e^+$ distinguishes germ-track as a theorem; no large-$e$ observation distinguishes mirage as a theorem. The empirical germ-track signature is a bounded, stabilized defect and delay along one compatible chain, eventually with $D\ge2e^++1$. The empirical mirage signature is continued image contraction plus growing defect/loss, followed ultimately by EMPTY. A genuinely singular formal germ can imitate the latter until very deep order.
   393	
   394	A locus-wide claim that no D25 point has $e^+\le12$ requires symbolic stratification of every D25 component. Witness sampling cannot prove it. If the present \(\ell^+\ge31\) obstruction persists at a D25 point, then any finite-$e$ target for that point is at least D63; this is not itself evidence of nonextension.
