   526	## 5. The completed-ideal bridge
   527	
   528	There are two different bridge obligations: a filtered finite-depth bridge
   529	for the initial residual, and a full completed-ideal bridge for the final
   530	solution. Both live **before numerical evaluation**. After specialization to
   531	a point the coefficients are scalars, so a “coefficient ideal over \(k\)” is
   532	not the needed statement.
   533	
   534	Fix an admissible witness cylinder \(\mathscr B\), for example the Newton
   535	ball \(s+F^1X\), with its named base relations and chart units. For each
   536	global depth \(N\), let \(C_N\) be the localized finite-jet coordinate ring
   537	representing the allowed \(N\)-jets in \(\mathscr B\). It contains exactly
   538	the source coefficient variables that causality permits to affect raw
   539	coefficients of order \(<N\), modulo the named base and pin relations, and it
   540	inverts only the named chart units. Jet truncation is contravariant on
   541	coordinate rings: for \(M\ge N\) it gives a pullback \(C_N\to C_M\). Write
   542	
   543	\[
   544	 C_{\rm alg}=\varinjlim_N C_N,
   545	 \qquad
   546	 \widehat C=\varprojlim_\lambda C_{\rm alg}/\mathfrak a_\lambda,       \tag{5.1}
   547	\]
   548	
   549	where \((\mathfrak a_\lambda)\) is an explicitly declared defining filtration
   550	and \(\widehat C\) is required to be separated. Thus \(C_{\rm alg}\) is the
   551	ring of causal polynomial functions on finite jets, and \(\widehat C\) is a
   552	chosen completion—not an inverse limit of the jet coordinate rings. Require
   553	all pullbacks and universal coefficient functions to be compatible. Every
   554	formal point \(x\in\mathscr B\) gives evaluation maps, compatible under
   555	pullback,
   556	
   557	\[
   558	                         \operatorname{ev}_{x,N}:C_N\to k.             \tag{5.2}
   559	\]
   560	
   561	### Proposition 5.1 (universal coefficient bridge under CYCLIC-30)
   562	
   563	Let \(A\) be a commutative ring. Suppose the universal identity
   564	
   565	\[
   566	 \mathcal E=\sum_{a=0}^{29}t^{s_a}H_a(u)\eta^a,
   567	 \qquad H_a(u)=\sum_{j\ge0}h_{a,j}u^j,                  \tag{5.3}
   568	\]
   569	
   570	holds in \(A[[t]][\eta]\), with every higher \(\eta\)-component identically
   571	zero. Then
   572	
   573	\[
   574	 [t^n\eta^a]\mathcal E=
   575	 \begin{cases}
   576	 h_{a,j},&0\le a\le29,\ n=s_a+6j,\ j\ge0,\\
   577	 0,&\text{otherwise}.
   578	 \end{cases}                                             \tag{5.4}
   579	\]
   580	
   581	Consequently, in \(A\), the pristine coefficient ideal is
   582	
   583	\[
   584	 I_E^+=\bigl(h_{a,j}:0\le a\le29,\ j\ge0\bigr),          \tag{5.5}
   585	\]
   586	
   587	and its part below depth \(D\) is
   588	
   589	\[
   590	 I_{E,<D}^+=\bigl(h_{a,j}:s_a+6j<D\bigr).                \tag{5.6}
   591	\]
   592	
   593	#### Proof
   594	
   595	Substitute the \(u\)-expansions into (5.3) and use \(u=t^6\). Uniqueness of
   596	coefficients in \(A[[t]][\eta]\) gives (5.4), hence (5.5)--(5.6).
   597	\(\square\)
   598	
   599	The relevant instances are the truncated statement over \(A=C_N\) and the
   600	all-depth statement over \(A=C_{\rm alg}\) or its declared completion, not the
   601	already evaluated field. Under literal `CYCLIC-30`, Proposition 5.1 supplies
   602	the raw coefficient bridge. If `CYCLIC-30` is weakened, `BRIDGE-30` must
   603	additionally supply universal membership identities for every higher
   604	\(\eta\)-component.
   605	
   606	### Lemma 5.2 (levelwise ideal equality gives completed equality)
   607	
   608	Let \(C\) be a separated complete linearly topologized ring with defining
   609	ideals \(\mathfrak a_N\), and let \(I,J\subseteq C\). If
   610	
   611	\[
   612	 (I+\mathfrak a_N)/\mathfrak a_N
   613	   =(J+\mathfrak a_N)/\mathfrak a_N\quad\text{for every }N, \tag{5.7}
   614	\]
   615	
   616	then
   617	
   618	\[
   619	                         \overline I=\overline J.         \tag{5.8}
   620	\]
   621	
   622	#### Proof
   623	
   624	For a linear topology,
   625	
   626	\[
   627	 \overline I=\bigcap_N(I+\mathfrak a_N),\qquad
   628	 \overline J=\bigcap_N(J+\mathfrak a_N).
   629	\]
   630	
   631	Equation (5.7) says \(I+\mathfrak a_N=J+\mathfrak a_N\) for each \(N\), so
   632	the intersections agree. \(\square\)
   633	
   634	Completeness is used to realize \(C\) as the intended inverse-limit
   635	coefficient algebra; the displayed closure formula itself only needs the
   636	stated linear topology.
   637	
   638	For a direct, evaluation-safe bridge, let \(h_N\) be the finite vector of
   639	the universal selected coefficients \(h_{a,j}\) of order \(<N\), and let
   640	\(g_N\) be the finite vector of all pristine raw equations of order \(<N\),
   641	both in \(C_N\). `BRIDGE-30` must give rectangular matrices over \(C_N\)
   642	
   643	\[
   644	                 g_N=U_Nh_N,\qquad h_N=V_Ng_N,           \tag{5.9}
   645	\]
   646	
   647	compatible after pullback to every deeper jet ring, with every denominator a
   648	named chart unit. The
   649	first identity is the implication needed after Newton; the second proves
   650	equality of ideals in each \(C_N\), hence in \(C_{\rm alg}\); their closures
   651	then agree in every declared separated completion. The same two-sided
   652	identities must connect any emitted Schur/pivot row vector to the pristine
   653	one. Exact reconstruction and direct pristine-row replay are an alternative.
   654	
   655	### Proposition 5.3 (the levelwise bridge transfers a formal zero)
   656	
   657	Assume the first identity in (5.9) for every \(N\). If a formal point
   658	\(x\in\mathscr B\) satisfies every selected coefficient \(h_{a,j}(x)=0\),
   659	then every pristine equation vanishes at \(x\).
   660	
   661	#### Proof
   662	
   663	For each \(N\), evaluate the identity \(g_N=U_Nh_N\) using (5.2). Its
   664	right-hand side is zero, so every pristine coefficient of order \(<N\) is
   665	zero. Since \(N\) is arbitrary, all pristine coefficients vanish.
   666	\(\square\)
   667	
   668	This finite-level proof, not closure equality alone, is the safe vanishing
   669	argument: evaluation at an infinite tail point need not have closed kernel
   670	for an arbitrary tail topology. Lemma 5.2 records the completed-ideal equality
   671	that (5.9) also proves inside the declared completion \(\widehat C\) of (5.1).
   672	
   673	The initial residual must likewise be recomputed directly by (1.11), or from
   674	a filtration-triangular identity; an arbitrary presentation change can mix
   675	levels. Equality of radicals, equality of point sets, or one-way reduction is
   676	insufficient. Radical, saturation, Rabinowitsch, pivot-definition, and
   677	`W`-pin equations are fixed base-chart conditions, not extra tail-function
   678	rows; reconstruction must show that they remain satisfied on \(\mathscr B\).
   679	
   680	## 6. Conditional Euler/Ore lifting theorem for this campaign
   681	
   682	### Theorem 6.1 (corrected 30-stream germ certificate)
   683	
   684	Fix a coefficient field \(k\), a named radical/chart branch, `PIN42`, and all
   685	other held-fixed base data. Let \(s_D\) be a depth-\(D\) point. Suppose a
   686	certificate supplies:
   687	
   688	1. a legal full source completion \(s\) of \(s_D\);
   689	2. the source-dependent all-depth map on \(s+F^1X\), together with
   690	   `CYCLIC-30`, or the surplus-membership alternative in `BRIDGE-30`, as
   691	   universal identities on that whole ball;
   692	3. the exact residual check \(\mathcal H(s)\in F^DY^+\);
   693	4. the exact derivative \(L_s^+=D\mathcal H_s\), independently replayed from
   694	   (1.6);
   695	5. a causal right section
   696	
   697	   \[
   698	   S:F^eY^+\to X,\qquad L_s^+S=1,\qquad
   699	   S(F^{n+e}Y^+)\subseteq F^nX\quad(n\ge0);              \tag{6.1}
   700	   \]
   701	
   702	6. `FILTER-30` on \(s+F^1X\), including unit control for every localization;
   703	7. the levelwise pristine/emitted identities (5.9) of `BRIDGE-30` throughout
   704	   that ball; and
   705	8. \(D\ge2e+1\).
   706	
   707	Then there is an allowed formal tail tuple
   708	
   709	\[
   710	 s_\infty\in s+F^{D-e}X                               \tag{6.2}
   711	\]
   712	
   713	over \(k[[t]]\) satisfying the full pristine formal equation system on the
   714	named chart. It agrees with the supplied finite point only below depth
   715	\(D-e\); “lifts” here means lifting that shorter truncation. Hence a scoped
   716	mod-\(p\) formal germ exists, but not necessarily one with the entire
   717	depth-\(D\) jet \(s_D\).
   718	
   719	#### Proof
   720	
   721	`FILTER-30` and Lemma 4.2 give (3.2)--(3.3) with \(\sigma=0\). Theorem 3.1 applied to
   722	\(\mathcal H\), \(L_s^+\), and (6.1) produces
   723	\(s_\infty=s+h_\infty\) with all 30 \(H_a\) zero and with (6.2).
   724	The point \(s_\infty\) remains in \(s+F^1X\). Proposition 5.3, applied to the
   725	universal `BRIDGE-30` identities, makes every pristine formal equation vanish.
   726	The corrections lie only in \(X\), so all held-fixed chart conditions and pins
   727	remain fixed, and the certified chart denominators remain units. \(\square\)
   728	
   729	The proof uses the one operator \(L_s^+\) throughout. There is no additional
   730	requirement that right inverses at the Newton iterates be stable.
   731	
   732	## 7. Exact certificate contract
   733	
   734	An implementation should report the following, with exact identities rather
   735	than only hashes or finite samples.
   736	
   737	### 7.1 Scope and completion
   738	
   739	- coefficient field, prime/extension, \(t=x^{-1/42}\), and \(u=t^6\);
   740	- depth \(D\), branch, chart units, frozen data, pins, witness, and
   741	  reconstruction provenance;
   742	- every coefficient of the chosen full completion in a finite symbolic,
   743	  rational, recurrent, or otherwise exactly evaluable representation;
   744	- the universal source-dependent rule for the actual \(t^{42+}\) x-side
   745	  factors under every tail variation in \(s+F^1X\), not merely their values
   746	  and first derivatives at \(s\).
   747	
   748	For D23/D25 reconstruction, the banked DEEPMAP true-name registry is part of
   749	that provenance and must be replayed canonically:
   750	
   751	```text
   752	x74=tg02_54  x75=tg01_54  x76=tg2_54   x77=tg2_49
   753	x78=tg1_54   x79=tg1_49   x80=tf2_54   x81=tf2_49
   754	x82=tf1_54   x83=tf1_49
   755	```
   756	
   757	The old swapped names are import-only aliases, not matrix labels.
   758	
   759	An arbitrary zero completion of genuinely free source coordinates is allowed
   760	only if it is named and the **full** equation and derivative are recomputed
   761	there. Zeroing the omitted x-side correction in the pure-y constructor is not
   762	such a completion.
   763	
   764	### 7.2 Source and residual
   765	
   766	- all 30 input and 30 output labels, their order, and shifts (1.0)--(1.4);
   767	- an all-depth `CYCLIC-30` proof, or the universal levelwise
   768	  surplus-membership alternative of `BRIDGE-30` for every additional output;
   769	- the raw label bijection
   770	
   771	  \[
   772	  (n,a)\longleftrightarrow
   773	  \left(a,\frac{n-s_a}{6}\right);
   774	  \]
   775	
   776	  here \(0\le a\le29\), \(n\ge s_a\), and
   777	  \(n\equiv s_a\pmod 6\);
   778	
   779	- exact replay of every raw coefficient below \(D\), giving
   780	
   781	  \[
   782	  \nu:=\nu_Y(\mathcal H(s))\ge D.                        \tag{7.1}
   783	  \]
   784	
   785	  If the starting point was certified only in emitted rows, a direct replay
   786	  or filtration-triangular finite-level bridge must establish (7.1).
   787	
   788	### 7.3 Linear certificate
   789	
   790	- the exact all-depth Ore coefficients of \(L_s^+\), with the operator tied to
   791	  the same completion as the residual;
   792	- causality in the global \(t\)-filtration;
   793	- an exact description of \(S\) and proofs, on every target basis stream, of
   794	
   795	  \[
   796	  L_s^+S=I,\qquad
   797	  \nu_X(Sy)\ge\nu_Y(y)-e\quad(\nu_Y(y)\ge e);             \tag{7.2}
   798	  \]
   799	
   800	- for a recurrence certificate: a finite symbolic rule parameterized by the
   801	  target basis index \(j\), its memory and initial transient, an invariant
   802	  state space, and identities proving (7.2) for all \(j\). A finite period may
   803	  replace the all-\(j\) proof only after the certificate proves that the full
   804	  operator coefficients and transition data—not merely the scalar \(j\)
   805	  occurring in \(\Theta u^j=ju^j\)—are periodic or finite-state, and verifies
   806	  every boundary state.
   807	
   808	Neither bounded \(\delta^+(N)\) nor its apparent stabilization proves (7.2).
   809	
   810	### 7.4 Presentation and final inequality
   811	
   812	- one finite symbolic rule producing the compatible two-sided identities
   813	  (5.9) for arbitrary \(N\), or direct universal reconstruction/replay; a
   814	  finite list of unrelated sampled matrices is not a proof for every level;
   815	- the `FILTER-30` syntax/unit audit invoking Lemma 4.2; and
   816	- the sharp decisive check
   817	
   818	  \[
   819	                         \boxed{\nu-2e\ge1}.              \tag{7.3}
   820	  \]
   821	
   822	  If the advertised certificate records only a guaranteed depth \(D\le\nu\),
   823	  the directly checkable sufficient form is
   824	
   825	  \[
   826	             \boxed{\nu\ge D\quad\text{and}\quad 2e+1\le D}. \tag{7.4}
   827	  \]
   828	
   829	If a normalization audit finds a loss \(\sigma>0\), replace (7.3) by
   830	\(\nu-2e-\sigma\ge1\), or the second inequality in (7.4) by
   831	\(2e+\sigma+1\le D\).
   832	
   833	## 8. What \(e^+\) should mean
   834	
   835	First define the Round-6 diagnostics without importing conventions from
   836	another file. Strip the shifts from an input as
   837	\(x_q=t^{r_q}\sum_{j\ge0}x_{q,j}u^j\), and likewise strip \(t^{s_a}\) from
   838	the output. Causality makes the first \(N\) normalized output coefficients
   839	depend only on the first \(N\) normalized input coefficients. In the ordered
   840	bases \((q,j)\), \((a,j)\), \(0\le j<N\), let
   841	
   842	\[
   843	 M^+(N):(k[u]/u^N)^{30}\longrightarrow(k[u]/u^N)^{30}   \tag{8.1}
   844	\]
   845	
   846	be the resulting \(30N\times30N\) matrix of \(L_s^+\), and put
   847	
   848	\[
   849	                  \delta^+(N)=30N-\operatorname{rank}M^+(N).          \tag{8.2}
   850	\]
   851	
   852	The symbol \(d^+\) may be recorded only when an exact all-depth recurrence or
   853	Ore normal form proves that some integer \(N_0\) satisfies
   854	
   855	\[
   856	                  \delta^+(N)=d^+\quad\text{for every }N\ge N_0.     \tag{8.3}
   857	\]
   858	
   859	A long constant sample is not (8.3). Even (8.3) does not itself construct a
   860	section.
   861	
   862	The Newton theorem does not use this defect/index diagnostic. Let
   863	\(\ell^+=\ell(L_s^+)\) be the minimal loss (2.1), and let
   864	
   865	\[
   866	 e^+_{\rm cert}:=\text{any proved upper bound on \(\ell^+\) realized by
   867	 a section satisfying (7.2)}.                              \tag{8.4}
   868	\]
   869	
   870	It is safest to retain two separate fields:
   871	
   872	```text
   873	E_LOSS_CERT     = e_cert_plus
   874	E_INDEX         = 6*d_plus - 12       # diagnostic only
   875	```
   876	
   877	If (8.3) is proved, the corrected index diagnostic is
   878	
   879	\[
   880	 (e^+)^{\rm idx}=6d^++\sum_as_a-\sum_qr_q=6d^+-12.       \tag{8.5}
   881	\]
   882	
   883	The legacy convention may call this number \(e^+\), but it becomes a
   884	conservative Newton certificate only when the same exact normal form also
   885	proves a section with
   886	
   887	\[
   888	 0\le\ell^+\le(e^+)^{\rm idx}.                           \tag{8.6}
   889	\]
   890	
   891	Merely proving (8.3), computing (8.5), and checking a weighted pivot sum is
   892	not sufficient. Conversely, a direct section of loss \(e\) proves a lift
   893	using (7.3) even when the index is larger or unavailable.
   894	
   895	For a residual known only to depth \(D\), the nominal thresholds are:
   896	
   897	| guaranteed depth | theorem gate using minimal loss | implementer check | conservative index route |
   898	|---:|---:|---:|---:|
   899	| \(23\) | \(\ell^+\le11\) | \(e^+_{\rm cert}\le11\) | \(\ell^+\le(e^+)^{\rm idx}\le11\) |
   900	| \(25\) | \(\ell^+\le12\) | \(e^+_{\rm cert}\le12\) | \(\ell^+\le(e^+)^{\rm idx}\le12\) |
   901	| \(D\) | \(\ell^+\le\lfloor(D-1)/2\rfloor\) | \(e^+_{\rm cert}\le\lfloor(D-1)/2\rfloor\) | same with the proved index upper bound |
   902	
   903	At the boundary values, the D23 correction lies in \(F^{12}X\), while the
   904	D25 correction lies in \(F^{13}X\). Smaller losses preserve correspondingly
   905	more of the supplied point; neither boundary case preserves the whole D23 or
   906	D25 jet.
   907	
   908	Since \((e^+)^{\rm idx}=6d^+-12\), the conservative D25 route permits only
   909	\(d^+=2,3,4\), giving indices \(0,6,12\); D23 permits only \(d^+=2,3\).
   910	Those integer restrictions do not replace PARAM-30.
   911	
   912	These table entries use only the advertised depth. The exact, sharper
   913	implementation is always (7.3): extra residual vanishing \(\nu>D\) permits a
   914	larger certified loss up to \(\lfloor(\nu-1)/2\rfloor\).
   915	
   916	Round 6's finite-window rank computation, together with its causality check
   917	that inputs above band 40 cannot affect degree 36, puts the degree-36 target
   918	\(t^{36}e_{29}\) outside the full image \(L_s^+(X)\) at 36 sampled operators.
   919	Taking \(n=6\) in (2.1) gives its stated valid bound \(\ell^+\ge31\). With the
   920	literal \(n\ge0\) convention in (2.1), the same fact gives the following
   921	**new strengthening** of that banked bound:
   922	
   923	\[
   924	                              \boxed{\ell^+\ge37}:        \tag{8.7}
   925	\]
   926	
   927	for every \(e\le36\), that target lies in \(F^eY^+\) but not in \(L_s^+(X)\).
   928	This concerns exactly six witnesses times three deep draws times two primes
   929	on the single `a00pp` radical fiber—not 36 atlas fibers, and not unsampled
   930	D25 completions.
   931	
   932	Thus those sampled operators fail the nominal D23/D25 depth-only gate. They
   933	could pass (7.3) only at a completion with actual residual order at least 75,
   934	which would itself be a depth-75 point. A certificate using only that depth-75
   935	guarantee would require \(e^+_{\rm cert}\le37\); for \(\nu>75\), the exact
   936	allowance is instead \(e^+_{\rm cert}\le\lfloor(\nu-1)/2\rfloor\). In every
   937	case all other gates are still required, and the lower bound (8.7) supplies
   938	neither a section nor a germ.
   939	
   940	At D25:
   941	
   942	- family-wide EMPTY kills the scoped formal germ without any Newton lemma;
   943	- one named NONEMPTY survivor with one legal full completion at which the
   944	  residual, derivative, `CYCLIC-30` (or its bridge alternative), `BRIDGE-30`,
   945	  `FILTER-30`, `PARAM-30` of loss at most \(12\), and (7.4) are all certified
   946	  proves a scoped mod-\(p\) formal germ by Theorem 6.1;
   947	- NONEMPTY without those certificates is only finite-depth survival.
   948	
   949	## 9. Minimal remaining lemma list
   950	
   951	Everything below is an application gate, not a gap in Theorem 3.1.
   952	
   953	### CONJECTURE CYCLIC-30 (literal all-depth support/source generation)
   954	
   955	Universally on the admissible source ball, the full orbit products, including
   956	every normalized x-side term beginning at \(t^{42}\), satisfy
   957	
   958	\[
   959	 \mathcal E=\sum_{a=0}^{29}t^{s_a}H_a(u)\eta^a             \tag{9.1}
   960	\]
   961	
   962	identically, with the asserted congruence classes and with every
   963	\(\eta^a\)-component for \(a\ge30\) identically zero. This is Round 6's
   964	`CYCLIC-30` gate. The current band-41 regression does not prove it. The
   965	discovery of \(H_{29}\) after the old 29-stream assertion is the concrete
   966	warning against extrapolating the regression.
   967	
   968	Literal `CYCLIC-30` is stronger than the lifting theorem needs. Its weakest
   969	sufficient replacement is the universal **surplus part of `BRIDGE-30`**:
   970	retain the first 30 streams as \(\mathcal H\), and provide a finite symbolic
   971	rule expressing every higher component coefficient in their levelwise ideal.
   972	That replacement must not be reported as `CYCLIC-30`.
   973	
   974	### CONJECTURE BRIDGE-30 (pristine/emitted ideal bridge)
   975	
   976	In the universal finite jet rings \(C_N\) on the whole Newton ball, the ideal
   977	of the full pristine depth tower equals the levelwise ideal generated by the
   978	30 \(H_a\), through the compatible two-sided identities (5.9). If literal
   979	`CYCLIC-30` fails, these identities also include every surplus \(\eta\)-row.
   980	Every emitted Schur/pivot presentation is connected to the pristine vector by
   981	the same kind of identities over named chart units. Set-theoretic equality,
   982	radical equality, and identities only after evaluation at \(s\) are
   983	insufficient.
   984	
   985	`CYCLIC-30` proves the raw coefficient part through Proposition 5.1. The
   986	reconstruction/presentation part still needs its own certificate.
   987	
   988	### CONJECTURE FILTER-30 (zero nonlinear filtration loss)
   989	
   990	On \(s+F^1X\), the actual source-dependent all-depth normalized orbit
   991	products—including the \(t^{42+}\) x-side terms—are restricted
   992	Euler-differential power series with coefficients of nonnegative global
   993	\(t\)-order in the precise restricted sense following Lemma 4.2. Every
   994	localized denominator is a named order-zero unit and satisfies the filtered
   995	variation estimates (4.4), and its defining expression has its own
   996	zero-loss quadratic remainder as required in the inverse paragraph after
   997	Lemma 4.2. Equivalently, the certificate may directly prove (3.2)--(3.3) with
   998	\(\sigma=0\). Lemma 4.2 then discharges the nonlinear estimate; this gate is
   999	an audit of the repository formula, not a missing Newton argument. If the
  1000	audit instead finds loss \(\sigma\), use \(\nu>2e+\sigma\).
  1001	
  1002	### CONJECTURE PARAM-30 (pointwise all-depth Ore section)
  1003	
  1004	For any point advertised as `LIVE`, its fully specified corrected operator
  1005	\(L_s^+\) admits an exact causal right section satisfying (7.2) with the
  1006	advertised finite loss. A proof must close the initial transient and every
  1007	\(p\)-periodic resonance. No current `valuation_e2.py` artifact does this for
  1008	the corrected square object; its primary computation remains the obsolete
  1009	29-column blocks with an appended \(H_{29}\) diagnostic.
  1010	
  1011	### Required data, not a conjecture: legal completion
  1012	
  1013	A finite D25 point does not specify the all-depth operator. The certificate
  1014	must give a legal full completion, a sufficiently long compatible lift plus a
  1015	proved finite-determinacy bound, or a uniform parametrix over the quantified
  1016	completion variables. Silent zero-fill is not a proof.
  1017	
  1018	Once these four conjectural gates and the completion data are supplied at a
  1019	point, no further differential-Hensel lemma is missing: Theorem 6.1 promotes
  1020	the point exactly under (7.3), with (7.4) as its depth-only implementation.

