     6	## Executive verdict
     7	
     8	The global question is **not decided**: no point of the D23 window has yet
     9	been proved to exist, and neither an algebraizing Keller pair nor a unit-ideal
    10	certificate for the whole window is known.
    11	
    12	Three sharper conclusions are proved here.
    13	
    14	1. **Bounded algebraicity cannot kill D23.**  Every allowed D23 pole prefix
    15	   extends to a polynomial relation in the full residue-A support rectangle
    16	   $(\deg_x,\deg_y)=(42,126)$, and the recorded g-orbits simultaneously extend
    17	   to one in $(63,189)$.  Primitive exact-degree versions preserve every
    18	   coefficient through level 54.  Thus the forced low tails, the six no-log
    19	   pins, and the $-42$ Row-20 inhomogeneity impose no Hermite--Padé
    20	   obstruction at this depth.
    21	2. **Row 24 is not a new principal resonance.**  Its exact first-occurrence
    22	   symbol on the ten effective frontier tails has rank 4, just as in the
    23	   stable post-Row-12 regime.  The $b_2$ information can only enter the
    24	   nonlinear compatibility residual.  No Row-24 kill has been proved.
    25	3. **The literal banked B-zero window is disjoint from the Q2-l12 tier.**
    26	   On leaf 11, four Q2 quotient rows have an exact characteristic-zero
    27	   combination equal to a nonzero multiple of the saturated variable
    28	   `s1F`; hence that ordinary ideal is the unit ideal.  Leaves 12 and 13
    29	   are already domain-disjoint from $B=0$, and the origin is the banked
    30	   empty l13 stratum.  This is a genuine cross-family elimination, but its
    31	   scope is $V_{\rm bank}\cap Q2_{l12}$, not all residue A.
    32	
    33	The useful next junction is therefore mixed, not algebraicity alone: finish
    34	the finite Row-24--41 compatibility ladder, add the x-side at Row 42, and
    35	intersect the remaining Q2 strata.  For the canonical orbit completions
    36	below, the first separate support equations occur naturally at root levels
