   689	2. the source-dependent all-depth map on \(s+F^1X\), together with
   690	   `CYCLIC-30`, or the surplus-membership alternative in `BRIDGE-30`, as
   691	   universal identities on that whole ball;
   692	3. the exact residual check \(\mathcal H(s)\in F^DY^+\);
   693	4. the exact derivative \(L_s^+=D\mathcal H_s\), independently replayed from
   694	   (1.6);
   695	5. a causal right section
   696	
   697	   \[
   698	   S:F^eY^+\to X,\qquad L_s^+S=1,\qquad
   699	   S(F^{n+e}Y^+)\subseteq F^nX\quad(n\ge0);              \tag{6.1}
   700	   \]
   701	
   702	6. `FILTER-30` on \(s+F^1X\), including unit control for every localization;
   703	7. the levelwise pristine/emitted identities (5.9) of `BRIDGE-30` throughout
   704	   that ball; and
   705	8. \(D\ge2e+1\).
   706	
   707	Then there is an allowed formal tail tuple
   708	
   709	\[
   710	 s_\infty\in s+F^{D-e}X                               \tag{6.2}
   711	\]
   712	
   713	over \(k[[t]]\) satisfying the full pristine formal equation system on the
   714	named chart. It agrees with the supplied finite point only below depth
   715	\(D-e\); “lifts” here means lifting that shorter truncation. Hence a scoped
   716	mod-\(p\) formal germ exists, but not necessarily one with the entire
   717	depth-\(D\) jet \(s_D\).
   718	
   719	#### Proof
   720	
   721	`FILTER-30` and Lemma 4.2 give (3.2)--(3.3) with \(\sigma=0\). Theorem 3.1 applied to
   722	\(\mathcal H\), \(L_s^+\), and (6.1) produces
   723	\(s_\infty=s+h_\infty\) with all 30 \(H_a\) zero and with (6.2).
   724	The point \(s_\infty\) remains in \(s+F^1X\). Proposition 5.3, applied to the
   725	universal `BRIDGE-30` identities, makes every pristine formal equation vanish.
   726	The corrections lie only in \(X\), so all held-fixed chart conditions and pins
