   290	## 3. Higher rows: exact law, Row 24, and the ceiling
   291	
   292	### Proposition 3.1 (the $C_6$ grading law)
   293	
   294	For every pure-y J row, a nonzero coefficient
   295	$\operatorname{Row}_k[\eta^q]$ satisfies
   296	
   297	\[
   298	 k\equiv 2(q+1)\pmod 6. \tag{3.1}
   299	\]
   300	
   301	In particular every odd row vanishes identically.
   302	
   303	#### Proof
   304	
   305	Let $\omega=\zeta^7$, of order six.  In a through-direction size-42
   306	block, an $\eta^n$ coefficient selects $r=6-n$ root-series terms.  If
   307	their total relative slot is $s$, cycling the six roots multiplies the
   308	term by
   309	
   310	\[
   311	 \omega^{\sum_a(32+s_a)}.
   312	\]
   313	
   314	The selector sum is nonzero only when $2r+s\equiv0\pmod 6$, equivalently
   315	$s\equiv2n\pmod 6$.  A size-21 block has three roots and even levels; its
   316	order-three selector gives the same congruence.  In an off-direction $\Delta$
   317	block, the Newton power sums retain slots divisible by six, while each
   318	$\eta t^{20}$ insertion contributes $20\equiv2\pmod 6$.  Products
   319	preserve the weight.  Finally, $\eta$ differentiation in the J operator lowers
   320	the $\eta$ degree by one, yielding (3.1).  $\square$
   321	
   322	The registry adds four ordinary `tf/tg` tails at every absolute level and
   323	two `tg0` tails at every even level.  Thus every six new levels add exactly
   324	
   325	\[
   326	 6\cdot4+3\cdot2=30
   327	\]
   328	
   329	P/G variables.  For even $12\le k<42$, the effective first-occurrence block
   330	has ten variables: four odd tails at level $k+27$, first seen by pairing
   331	with the fixed pole slot 5, and six even tails at level $k+32$, seen
   332	directly at jet slot $k$.
   333	
   334	This is not, by itself, a proved 29-equation periodicity law.  Off-direction
   335	$\eta t^{20}$ insertions can raise the $\eta$-degree later in the pure-y
   336	window; the exact congruence (3.1) survives, but a uniform top-degree
   337	cancellation for every nonlinear frozen-B row has not been proved.  The
   338	banked rows through 22 show the $(9,10,10)$ component cycle, and the exact
   339	Row-24 frontier has nine components, but extrapolating that count forever
   340	would be a conjecture.
   341	
   342	As a guarded computational census, two primes and three generic seeds agree
   343	that Rows 24,26,...,40 have respectively
   344	
   345	\[
   346	 9,10,10,9,10,10,10,10,10
   347	\]
   348	
   349	components: 88 equations against 90 first-occurrence variables.  The no-log
   350	pins remove the otherwise present Row-30 $\eta^{29}$ term, while an
   351	$\eta^{29}$ term returns at Row 36 through unpinned level-48 discrepancies.
   352	This is evidence against an equation-growth kill in the remaining pure-$y$
   353	window, not a characteristic-zero theorem and not an existence proof.
   354	
   355	### Proposition 3.2 (exact Row-24 first-occurrence symbol)
   356	
   357	On the B-frozen chart, the Row-24 frontier is
   358	
   359	\[
   360	\begin{split}
   361	&\mathit{tf1}_{51},\mathit{tf2}_{51},\mathit{tg1}_{51},\mathit{tg2}_{51},\\
   362	&\mathit{tf1}_{56},\mathit{tf2}_{56},\mathit{tg1}_{56},\mathit{tg2}_{56},
   363	 \mathit{tg01}_{56},\mathit{tg02}_{56}.
   364	\end{split}
   365	\]
   366	
   367	Its exact nine-by-ten symbol, on $\eta$ powers $2,5,\ldots,26$, has rank four
   368	over the étale coefficient algebra, uniformly on all $h$-sign branches and
   369	all nonzero pole-scale fibers.  It factors polewise as
   370	
   371	\[
   372	 A_i^{\rm odd}(\eta)
   373	 \left(w_i\,\mathit{tf}_{i,51}-{2\over3}\mathit{hw}_i\,\mathit{tg}_{i,51}\right)
   374	 +A_i^{\rm even}(\eta)
   375	 \left(\mathit{tf}_{i,56}-{2\over3}\mathit{tg}_{i,56}
   376	       -{1\over3}\mathit{tg0}_{i,56}\right),
   377	 \tag{3.2}
   378	\]
   379	
   380	for $i=1,2$, with the four displayed $A$-vectors independent.  Unit
   381	pivots may be taken in `tf1_51,tf1_56,tf2_51,tf2_56`.
   382	
   383	#### Proof
   384	
   385	Pin every older free coefficient to zero, retaining only the ten variables
   386	above, and build the depth-25 products with the full exact variable-degree
   387	cap 25.  This computes the true first-occurrence symbol, not a differential
   388	approximation: a level-56 tail can pair only with slot zero, while a
   389	level-51 tail first appears with the fixed slot-5 pole coefficient; no older
   390	free can enter either coefficient.  Direct raw-ring comparison gives the
   391	ratios in (3.2).  Exact unit-pivot elimination gives rank four and no
   392	leftover on all four sign branches and at pole scales $(1,1)$, $(2,3)$, and
   393	$(1/5,7)$; the factorization shows the scale-uniform statement.  The
   394	canonical 90-entry symbol has SHA-256
   395	`ab5ee038b118ba6d0b6303c6b2b55b110dc9872c203e1c6b2d60044458e69d29`.
   396	$\square$
   397	
   398	For a fixed D23 point, the four level-51 values are already recorded dummy
   399	coordinates, so only the six new level-56 variables remain adjustable and
   400	their sub-symbol has rank two.  Row 24 can therefore impose as many as seven
   401	compatibility conditions on that fixed point.  For the existential problem
   402	over all of $V$, the level-51 controls participate and the nine-component
   403	symbol leaves at most five compatibility residuals.  **No computation here
   404	shows that those residuals vanish or are inconsistent.**
   405	
   406	Nor is 24 a resonance of the lead operator from `xmodel/sol-thmB.md`:
   407	
   408	\[
   409	 L_k(h)=-2p\left(6ph'+(k-18)p'h\right).
   410	\]
   411	
   412	A polynomial homogeneous solution has $h\propto p^{(18-k)/6}$, so the
   413	polynomial resonant indices are $(0,6,12,18)$.  At $k=24$ the exponent is
   414	$-1$.  The template's $h_2/b_2$ datum may occur in the nonlinear Row-24
   415	source after lower-row reduction, but it does not create a principal-symbol
   416	rank drop.
   417	
   418	The no-log pins do not change this conclusion: they concern only the six
   419	level-42 variables.  Also, the current pure-y identity stops at Row 41;
   420	Rows 42 and above require the x-side factors.  Therefore the present builder
   421	cannot support a claim about conditions “forever.”
   422	
   423	### Proposition 3.3 (an all-orders scheme kill is finite)
   424	
   425	Let $I_\infty$ be the ideal generated by every row coefficient, pin, and
   426	template relation in the polynomial ring on all formal coefficients,
   427	including Rabinowitsch variables for required units.  If
   428	$1\in I_\infty$, then $1\in I_N$ for some finite depth $N$.
   429	
   430	#### Proof
   431	
   432	An ideal-membership identity
   433	
   434	\[
   435	 1=\sum_j a_jf_j
   436	
   437	\]
   438	
   439	is, by definition, a finite sum.  Only finitely many row generators occur,
   440	so they all lie below one finite depth.  Conversely, if every finite-depth
   441	ideal is proper, their increasing union is proper and is contained in a
   442	prime ideal, giving a compatible formal point over the prime's residue-field
   443	extension.  $\square$
   444	
   445	Thus “infinite codimension” is not an emptiness proof: the ideal
   446	$(u_1,u_2,\ldots)$ has infinite codimension and still has the origin.  For
   447	bounded-support polynomial pairs the ambient coefficient ring is finite
   448	type, making finite detection still more direct.  A higher-row attack must
   449	produce a concrete finite inconsistency; asymptotic growth alone cannot kill
   450	$V$.
