   904	## 6. Orbit count and D27+ gate
   905	
   906	The action on labels has trivial stabilizer, hence
   907	
   908	\[
   909	\#(\Lambda/G)=1,\qquad |G|=36.\tag{6.1}
   910	\]
   911	
   912	For every faithful emitted depth system, any isomorphism-invariant solver
   913	question—emptiness, dimension, degree, component count after corresponding
   914	base change, rank defect, or existence of a point—has the same answer on
   915	all 36 fibers.  A point or certificate on the representative transports
   916	explicitly by `T_g`.
   917	
   918	Thus the D27+ execution plan is:
   919	
   920	1. compile one representative, normally `a00pp`;
   921	2. verify the finite source-to-emission and character gates below;
   922	3. solve that representative once per prime;
   923	4. transport the result or certificate to the remaining 35 components.
   924	
   925	The potential reduction is
   926	
   927	\[
   928	36\to1\quad\text{per prime},\qquad
   929	72\to2\quad\text{for the two banked primes},\tag{6.2}
   930	\]
   931	
   932	or 97.22 percent fewer expensive per-fiber solves.  The primes themselves
   933	are not in the same orbit.
   934	
   935	> **CONJECTURE FUTURE-EMISSION FIDELITY.** A not-yet-built optimized D27+
   936	> presentation obtained by pivoting, Schur reduction, normal forms,
   937	> saturation, and gauge choices equals the localized pristine depth ideal
   938	> and satisfies (5.4).
   939	
   940	This gap is operational and finitely checkable.  A future compiler should
   941	fail closed unless it passes:
   942	
   943	1. an absolute-level weight registry for every retained variable and
   944	   selector;
   945	2. row homogeneity or the four generator-edge dictionary identities;
   946	3. transport of every nonzero pin, chart denominator, and saturation
   947	   polynomial;
   948	4. both ideal inclusions for each optimized pivot/Schur replacement;
   949	5. reduced-GB/NF round trips and leading-support checks; and
   950	6. one independent second-prime replay before promoting a cross-prime
   951	   structural claim.
   952	
   953	The raw all-depth theorem means a failure of one of these gates diagnoses
   954	the compiler/presentation; it is not evidence that mathematical
   955	equivariance failed.
   956	
   957	No action is claimed here between the two `r3` embeddings, between primes,
   958	after swapping pole charts, after unfreezing `B`, or on other infinity
   959	charts.  Those are separate symmetry or coverage questions.
