   192	## 3. Why the operator does not yet choose flat or growth
   193	
   194	### 3.1 D23 and D25 used the same window
   195	
   196	`cases/eplus_certify.py` fixes
   197	
   198	```text
   199	RMAX = 40
   200	window shape = 174 outputs x 170 inputs
   201	```
   202	
   203	and `gate_param30(E, p, D)` uses `D` only to compute the threshold
   204	(\lfloor(D-1)/2\rfloor). `cases/d25_eplus.py` reconstructs a D25 point and
   205	then calls that same gate. It does not append the (H_{29}u^1) row.
   206	
   207	Consequently, the two distributions `{37: ...}` mean:
   208	
   209	- the same low obstruction survived a broad change of sampled point and the
   210	  D25 frontier completion; and
   211	- no sampled D25 point acquired a section small enough for D25.
   212	
   213	They do **not** mean (\ell(23)=\ell(25)=37), do not give an upper bound 37,
   214	and do not estimate a depth derivative.
   215	
   216	### 3.2 The level-36 cokernel relation does not shift automatically
   217	
   218	In Ore normal form the entries have the structure
   219	
   220	\[
   220	\[
   221	 L_{aq}=\sum_{m\ge0}u^m(A_{aqm}+B_{aqm}\Theta),
   222	 \qquad \Theta u=u(\Theta+1),                               \tag{3.1}
   223	\]
   224	
   225	as recorded in `xmodel/sol-round5.md` §3. On an input coefficient (u^j),
   226	the diagonal factor is (A_{aqm}+jB_{aqm}). Equivalently,
   227	
   228	\[
   229	 L(uZ)=u\sum_{m\ge0}u^m\bigl((A_m+B_m)+B_m\Theta\bigr)Z,   \tag{3.2}
   230	\]
   231	
   232	not (uL(Z)). A left-cokernel relation at coefficient index (j=0) is
   233	therefore not automatically a relation at (j=1). At (j=1), the matrix
   234	coefficients change, prior coefficient columns can feed forward, and the
   235	normalized x-side begins.
   236	
   237	This gives the exact current ruling:
   238	
   239	> **CONJECTURE FLAT-H29.** After the level-36 transient, the corrected
   240	> all-depth operator has a causal right section of loss 37, so no deeper
   241	> target raises the floor.
   242	
   243	> **CONJECTURE SHIFTED-H29-BINDING.** The missing target extends to a proved
   244	> sequence of cokernel targets (y_j=t^{36+6j}e_{29}), or to another
   245	> cofinal obstruction sequence of comparable level.
   246	
   247	Neither conjecture follows from (3.1). The first new coefficient is the
   248	decisive one:
   249	
   250	\[
   251	                       y_1=t^{42}e_{29}.                            \tag{3.3}
   252	\]
   253	
   254	If every (y_j) in a depth window were certified missing, then for (D\ge37)
   255	the window would give
   256	
   257	\[
   258	 f(D)=37+6\left\lfloor\frac{D-37}{6}\right\rfloor.          \tag{3.4}
   259	\]
   260	
   261	Indeed, the largest included (H_{29}) level is
   262	(36+6\lfloor(D-37)/6\rfloor), and the (n=0) loss bound is one larger.
   263	Here (f(D)\ge D-5), so (2f(D)+1>D) throughout this range. For a fixed
   264	all-depth operator, missing all (y_j) would in fact give (\ell(L)=\infty).
   265	Equation (3.4) is a conditional consequence, not a current certificate.
