   668	## 6. Growth branch and the exact boundary of a kill theorem
   669	
   670	### 6.1 What a growing universal floor proves unconditionally
   671	
   672	Let (\mathcal Z_\infty) be the allowed formal zeros of the pristine scoped
   673	residue-A system. For each ladder depth (D), let (\mathcal C_D) contain
   674	every legal all-depth completion of every depth-D survivor in that same
   675	scope. Assume:
   676	
   677	1. a certified locus/all-completion floor
   678	   \[
   679	       \ell(D\mathcal H_s)\ge f(D)\qquad(s\in\mathcal C_D);   \tag{6.1}
   680	   \]
   681	2. (2f(D)+1>D) on an unbounded cofinal depth ladder; and
   682	3. every (z\in\mathcal Z_\infty), viewed as its own full completion, belongs
   683	   to (\mathcal C_D) through its D-jet for every ladder depth.
   684	
   685	The third item is the root-to-selected-system half of the universal
   686	`CYCLIC-30`/`BRIDGE-30` scope, not a consequence of sampling.
   687	
   688	### Theorem 6.1 (growth forces formal singularity)
   689	
   690	Under assumptions 1--3, every allowed formal zero has infinite delayed loss:
   691	
   692	\[
   693	                  z\in\mathcal Z_\infty
   694	                  \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
   695	                  \ell(D\mathcal H_z)=\infty.                \tag{6.2}
   696	\]
   697	
   698	#### Proof
   699	
   700	Suppose instead that (e=\ell(D\mathcal H_z)<\infty). Choose a ladder depth
   701	(D\ge2e+1). Since the exact completion (z) belongs to (\mathcal C_D),
   702	
   703	\[
   704	                         e\ge f(D).                            \tag{6.3}
   705	\]
   706	
   707	But (2f(D)+1>D\ge2e+1), so (f(D)>e), contradicting (6.3).
   708	\(\square\)
   709	
   710	Thus a growing universal floor proves:
   711	
   712	- no finite-loss, linearly regular formal germ exists in the scoped tower;
   713	- the promoted Newton sufficient criterion cannot fire on the exact
   714	  truncations of any formal root; and
   715	- if formal roots exist, all of them lie on an infinitely singular track.
   716	
   717	It does not yet prove (\mathcal Z_\infty=\varnothing).
   718	
   719	If **CONJECTURE SHIFTED-H29-BINDING** holds for every (y_j), then (3.4)
   720	supplies a concrete (f(D)) satisfying the hypotheses. At any fixed formal
   721	root it also directly makes the derivative loss infinite. This remains
   722	compatible with the existence of a singular root.
   723	
   724	### 6.2 Conditional KILL THEOREM
   725	
   726	The missing converse-side statement must be isolated rather than attributed
   727	to Newton:
   728	
   729	> **CONJECTURE FORMAL-REGULARITY-30.** Every allowed formal zero (z) of the
   730	> scoped pristine residue-A system has finite delayed derivative loss
   731	> (\ell(D\mathcal H_z)<\infty).
   732	
   733	### Theorem 6.2 (conditional H29 kill)
   734	
   735	Assume the three hypotheses of Theorem 6.1 and
   736	**CONJECTURE FORMAL-REGULARITY-30**. Then
   737	
   738	\[
   739	                              \mathcal Z_\infty=\varnothing.   \tag{6.4}
   740	\]
   741	
   742	#### Proof
   743	
   744	Theorem 6.1 says every member of (\mathcal Z_\infty) has infinite loss;
   745	formal regularity says every member has finite loss. Hence there is no
   746	member. \(\square\)
   747	
   748	No uniform upper bound on the losses is needed. Pointwise finiteness is
   749	enough, because the cofinal ladder can be chosen beyond (2e+1) separately
   750	for each hypothetical root.
   751	
   752	This regularity hypothesis is a genuine gap and is false for general
   753	filtered Euler equations. In characteristic (p),
   754	
   755	\[
   756	                         \mathcal H(x)=(\Theta+1)x             \tag{6.5}
   757	\]
   758	
   759	has the exact formal root (x=0), while its derivative misses
   760	(u^{p-1},u^{2p-1},\ldots) and has infinite loss. This is the promoted
   761	lemma's own resonance example in `xmodel/sol-newton-lemma.md` (4.5). In every
   762	characteristic, (\mathcal H(x)=x^2) has the exact root zero and zero
   763	derivative, again with infinite loss. Neither existence, Noetherianity,
   764	smoothness of the finite D25 cells, nor `PARAM-30` at one advertised point
   765	proves **CONJECTURE FORMAL-REGULARITY-30**.
   766	
   767	The unconditional kill remains a finite exhaustive inconsistency:
   768	(V_D=\varnothing) at one depth. `xmodel/sol-algkill.md` Proposition 3.3
   769	explains the algebraic boundary: if the all-orders ideal contains 1, a finite
   770	subsystem already contains 1; asymptotic codimension or loss growth alone is
   771	not emptiness.
   772	
   773	### 6.3 In what sense a true finite-loss root's truncation would certify
   774	
   775	There is a rigorous mathematical statement, but it is not automatically an
   776	effective compiler statement.
   777	
   778	Let (z\) be a true formal root with finite loss
   779	(e=\ell(D\mathcal H_z)). Lemma 2.1 of
   780	`xmodel/sol-newton-lemma.md` supplies an abstract causal section of delay
   781	(e). Take (D=2e+1), take the D-jet (z_D), and use (z) itself as the
   782	named legal full completion. Then:
   783	
   784	- the residual order is (\nu=\infty);
   785	- the exact derivative is (D\mathcal H_z);
   786	- the section has loss (e); and
   787	- (D\ge2e+1) holds with equality.
   788	
   789	Assuming the universal `CYCLIC-30`, `BRIDGE-30`, and `FILTER-30` identities,
   790	Theorem 6.1 of the promoted Newton document applies. Therefore the sentence
   791	“a true finite-loss formal solution has a depth-((2e+1)) truncation that
   792	would certify” is mathematically rigorous when the certificate is allowed to
   793	name the unknown root as its completion.
   794	
   795	It is circular and non-effective as a machine artifact. Lemma 2.1 constructs
   796	the section by infinitely many degreewise choices; the exact certificate
   797	contract requires a finite Ore identity or finite-state recurrence.
   798	
   799	> **CONJECTURE EFFECTIVE-PARAM-30.** Every finite-loss formal residue-A root
   800	> in scope admits a finitely representable section certificate of the required
   801	> Ore/recurrence form.
   802	
   803	This conjecture is unnecessary for the logical conditional kill, but is
   804	needed to promise that a finite compiler would discover the certificate.
   805	
   806	There is a second issue if a compiler uses a canonical or zero completion
   807	(s_D) rather than the exact root (z). The following perturbation lemma is
   808	the required bridge.
   809	
   810	### Lemma 6.3 (stability of a delayed section under a deep derivative change)
   811	
   812	Suppose (L_z) has a loss-(e) section (S), (s_D-z\in F^qX) with (q>e),
   813	and, for (K=L_{s_D}-L_z),
   814	
   815	\[
   816	                         K(F^nX)\subseteq F^{n+q}Y^+
   817	                         \quad(n\ge0).                       \tag{6.6}
   818	\]
   819	
   820	Then (L_{s_D}) has a right section with loss at most (e).
   821	
   822	#### Proof
   823	
   824	On (F^eY^+), the operator (KS) raises target filtration by (q-e>0).
   825	Therefore
   826	
   827	\[
   828	                    B=(I+KS)^{-1}=\sum_{j\ge0}(-KS)^j         \tag{6.7}
   829	\]
   830	
   831	converges and preserves every (F^{n+e}Y^+). Set (S_D=SB). Since
   832	
   833	\[
   834	                 L_{s_D}S=(L_z+K)S=I+KS,
   835	\]
   836	
   837	we have (L_{s_D}S_D=I), and the same delay estimate follows from those for
   838	(S) and (B). \(\square\)
   839	
   840	> **CONJECTURE TRUNCATION-STABILITY-30.** The actual normalized residue-A map
   841	> satisfies the derivative-Lipschitz estimate (6.6), and the compiler's
   842	> canonical depth-D completion is (F^q)-close to the true root with the
   843	> required (q>e) (ideally (q\ge D)).
   844	
   845	`FILTER-30` should be the source of the derivative estimate, but the x-side
   846	restricted-series audit and the exact source-depth identification are not
   847	promoted. Until this conjecture is proved, only the exact-root-completion
   848	argument above is rigorous.
   849	
   850	## 7. Campaign decision rule
   851	
   852	The next action is not another run of the band-40 scanner. It is the D43
   853	compiler of §4.
   854	
   855	1. If (H_{29}u^1) has a dual cokernel witness at a compatible D43 survivor,
   856	   the floor grows pointwise to at least 43. Repeat at D49 to test
   857	   (H_{29}u^2), and seek an all-index Ore/cokernel recurrence before making
   858	   a growth theorem.
   859	2. If (H_{29}u^1) is covered and no other new target is missed, record only
   860	   “flat through level 42.” Pursue the all-depth loss-37 section and the D75
   861	   point in parallel; neither finite observation proves exact flatness.
   862	3. If the scoped D43 scheme is exhaustively EMPTY, bank the finite-depth kill
   863	   and stop the loss campaign for that scope.
   864	4. If a cofinal growing floor is eventually proved, report Theorem 6.1
   865	   unconditionally and Theorem 6.2 only with
   866	   **CONJECTURE FORMAL-REGULARITY-30** visibly attached.
   867	
   868	The decisive distinction is therefore not “37 at D23 versus 37 at D25.” It
   869	is whether the corrected post-41 operator supplies a preimage or a new dual
   870	cokernel witness for (t^{42}e_{29}), with the real x-side present.

