+N_Y(D)&=\sum_a\max\!\left(0,
+ \left\lfloor\frac{D-1-s_a}{6}\right\rfloor+1\right),\\
+N_X(D)&=\sum_q\max\!\left(0,
+ \left\lfloor\frac{D-1-r_q}{6}\right\rfloor+1\right).
+\end{aligned}                                                   \tag{4.1}
+\]
+
+They give:
+
